{:edb/db-before-t 1965 :edb/db-after-t 1966 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535278 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:05:15.047Z" 13194139535278 true] [17592186105776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341233 13194139535278 true] [17592186105776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341240 13194139535278 true] [17592186105776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341261 13194139535278 true] [17592186105777 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341247 13194139535278 true] [17592186105777 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341254 13194139535278 true] [17592186341233 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341234 13194139535278 true] [17592186341233 1089 "q-126921" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341233 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535278 true] [17592186341233 1100 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3.$ Find the outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C.$" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341233 1113 #uuid "d45dd63c-10bf-5009-8d17-f860f39bde5a" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341233 1145 "We can parameterize $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{′}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}=\\sqrt{3},\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341235 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341236 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341237 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341238 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341239 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1041 "selection" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341235 13194139535278 true] [17592186341234 1110 #uuid "1f4786a8-145a-572c-aeef-afd1f4d4920f" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341235 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535278 true] [17592186341235 1111 #uuid "03e228b3-ea11-58a0-b53c-2fc041457b19" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341236 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535278 true] [17592186341236 1103 